From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: select the librecode converter by its registered name

License: GPL-2.0-only
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

Enca registers the in-process GNU recode backend as "librecode".  The TeX
regression first confirms that this backend is available, but then requests
the nonexistent converter name "recode".  Select "librecode" so the test
exercises the backend it just detected instead of failing during option
parsing.

This was reproduced by exact-head openEuler RISC-V CI run 31761326622.
Remove the patch when an upstream release carries the same converter name.

---
 test/test-tex.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/test-tex.sh b/test/test-tex.sh
--- a/test/test-tex.sh
+++ b/test/test-tex.sh
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ else
   if $ENCA --list converters | grep '^librecode$' >/dev/null; then
     TEST_TEXT=$srcdir/cs-s.tex
-    OPTS="-L cs -C recode"
+    OPTS="-L cs -C librecode"
     # File
     cp $TEST_TEXT $TESTNAME.actual
     $ENCA $OPTS -x UTF-8 $TESTNAME.actual || DIE=1
